{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Clarification on why the five held changes still fail e2e, and why the hold is still right\n\nMonitor fired on Gerrit run 33839579301. Checked rather than assumed: headSha 6125c5345f01, and\n'git merge-base --is-ancestor 668523feffde 6125c5345f01' says the 9a17 fix is NOT an ancestor. So it\npredates the fix and the pytest failure is expected. 9a17's closure stands.\n\nTHE NUANCE WORTH RECORDING, because it changes what 'the fix has landed' means for open changes:\nthe Verified lane takes WORKFLOWS from trusted main but TEST CODE from the patchset. Change 2600\ncontained both halves. So a patchset sitting on a pre-2600 base now gets the FIXED WORKFLOW -- whose\npre-provisioning step runs 'make -n e2e-deps', finds no such rule on that old tree, emits its\n::notice:: and skips -- and then falls back to the patchset's OWN conftest.py, which is still the old\nin-fixture provisioning that dies at the 300s cliff. The guard behaves exactly as designed; the point\nis that the fix is not retroactive.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: the five held changes (2594, 2601, 2607, 2608, 2609) need a REBASE to get the e2e fix at\nall -- not merely to clear the scanner job. My earlier framing implied the scanner was the only thing\nthe rebase was waiting on. It is both.\n\nThe hold is still correct, and for the same reason: rebasing now clears the e2e half but every one of\nthem would still fail scanner-integration, so none reaches Verified +1 and I would have spent five\nfull CI runs (~15-20 min each) to learn nothing. Rebase all five once the scanner fix lands, so a\nsingle round of CI can actually turn them green.\n\nExpect continued monitor noise from pre-fix runs draining out of the queue. Each is being checked\nagainst 'is 668523feffde an ancestor of this run's head' rather than assumed benign -- cheap, and it\nis the check that would catch a genuine recurrence."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788501388468756001,"uuid":"0eef229f-0fe8-4806-a4f2-53977bf60f32"}